      "response": "## Investigation report\n\nCitation integrity checked against saved evidence. Human review is required to assess the findings.\n\n### 1. Docs · Low\n\nThe code imports the Streamlit library as the alias \\`st\\`\\.\n\nSource: User supplied reproduction code · user\\_code · ev\\_13d26f5ece40cdf8d07859a166702937\n\n> import streamlit as st\n> \n> @st\\.cache\\_data\n> def load\\_rows\\(\\):\n>     return \\[1, 2, 3\\]\n> \n> st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\n\n### 2. Docs · Low\n\nA function named \\`load\\_rows\\` is defined and decorated with \\`@st\\.cache\\_data\\`\\.\n\nSource: User supplied reproduction code · user\\_code · ev\\_13d26f5ece40cdf8d07859a166702937\n\n> import streamlit as st\n> \n> @st\\.cache\\_data\n> def load\\_rows\\(\\):\n>     return \\[1, 2, 3\\]\n> \n> st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\n\n### 3. Docs · Low\n\n\\`load\\_rows\\` returns a static list \\`\\[1, 2, 3\\]\\`\\.\n\nSource: User supplied reproduction code · user\\_code · ev\\_13d26f5ece40cdf8d07859a166702937\n\n> import streamlit as st\n> \n> @st\\.cache\\_data\n> def load\\_rows\\(\\):\n>     return \\[1, 2, 3\\]\n> \n> st\\.write\\(load\\_rows\\(\\)\\)\n\n### Proposed next steps\n\n- Check that using \\`@st\\.cache\\_data\\` for a function that returns a constant list does not introduce unnecessary caching overhead or stale data concerns\\.\n",
